    "background_story": "Henry was a talented musician with a passion for sound and music. As a drummer in a local band, he spent countless hours perfecting his craft, but his love for loud music came at a cost. One fateful night, after a particularly energetic performance, Henry felt a searing pain in his ear. A trip to the doctor revealed that he had ruptured his eardrum, a devastating blow to his music career. Determined not to let his injury silence him, Henry learned to adapt, experimenting with new sounds and techniques that didn't rely on loud volumes. He discovered a new appreciation for the nuances of music and developed a unique style that showcased his creativity and resilience. Henry's experience taught him that even in the face of adversity, the music can still go on.",
